Ra2 44. h4 Ra4+ 45. Ke3 Rxf4 46. Kxf4 Kf6 $11 {and drawn with neither K having
an entry square}) 43... Ra3+ 44. Ke2 Rh3 45. Kf1 Rxh2 {though Bl has won a
pawn, it should still be a draw} 46. Kg1 Rh3 47. f3 h5 48. Kg2 (48. gxh5 Rxh5
$11 (48... gxh5 $2 49. Kg2 $18)) 48... hxg4 49. Rxg4 Rh6 50. Re4+ Kf6 51. Kg3
Rh5 52. Rf4+ Rf5 53. Ra4 e5 54. Ra6+ Kg5 55. Re6 Kh5 56. Re8 Kh6 57. Re7 Rg5+
58. Kf2 Rh5 59. Kg3 Rf5 60. Rd7 Kg5 61. Rd8 Kf6 62. Rd6+ Kf7 63. Rc6 Rf6 64.
Rc5 Ke6 65. Ra5 Kf5 66. Rb5 Rd6 67. Rb8 Rd3 68. Rf8+ Ke6 69. Re8+ Kf6 70. Kg4
Rd4+ 71. Kg3 Rf4 72. Rf8+ Kg5 73. Re8 Rf5 {20 moves without a cature or pawn
move} 74. Rxe5 Rxe5 75. f4+ Kf5 76. fxe5 Kxe5 77. Kg4 {the K & P ending is
also drawn as Bl needs his K to be in front of his pawn( and to have the
opposition)} Ke6 78. Kg5 Kf7 79. Kg4 Kg8 80. Kg5 Kg7 81. Kg4 Kf6 82. Kf4 g5+
83. Kg4 Kg6 84. Kg3 {falling back to the reserve blockade square each time} Kf5
85. Kf3 Ke5 86. Kg4 Kf6 87. Kg3 Kf5 88. Kf3 g4+ 89. Kg3 Kg5 90. Kg2 Kg6 91. Kg3
Kh5 92. Kg2 Kh4 93. Kh2 g3+ 94. Kg2 Kg4 95. Kg1 Kf3 96. Kf1 Kf4 97. Kg2 Kg4 98.
Kg1 Kh3 99. Kh1 g2+ 100. Kg1 Kg3 1/2-1/2

