$18 {SF16}) 14. Bxh6 (14. Ng5 {considered by Wh, the Engine shows how the
tactics are in Wh's favour} Nxe5 15. Bxe5 (15. h4 Nc6 16. Bxc6 dxc6 17. Ndxf7
Bxg5 18. hxg5 Kxf7 19. Be5 {SF16 also very strong}) 15... Bxg5+ 16. f4 Bf6 17.
Nxc8+ Rxc8 18. Rxd7+ Kf8 19. Rxb7 {SF16, Wh is a pawn up & Bl is scarcely
developed}) (14. Bg5+ Bxg5+ 15. Nxg5 Nxe5 16. f4 h6 17. Nxe6 Nd3+ 18. Rxd3 dxe6
19. Nxc8+ Rxc8 20. Rd7+ Kf6 21. Rxb7 $18 {SF16, is also good for Wh}) 14...
Nxh6 15. Bxc6 dxc6 16. Ng5 (16. Rd2 {SF16, just building up} b6 17. Rhd1 a5 18.
h3 Ra7 19. Ng5 $18) 16... Ng4 $5 {it looks as if Wh can virtually ignore this
single piece incursion} 17. Rde1 (17. Rhe1 Nxf2 18. Rd2 Ng4 19. Ngxf7 Rf8 20.
h3 Nh2 21. Rh1 $18 {SF16}) (17. Ngxf7 $1 Rf8 18. Rd4 h5 19. h3 c5 20. Rd2 $18 {
SF16}) 17... Nh6 18. Re4 (18. Rd1) 18... f6 19. Nxc8+ Raxc8 20. exf6+ Kxf6 21.
f4 (21. Nxe6 $18 {is simplest- Wh starting looking at attacking the K}) 21...
Rce8 22. Rhe1 e5 23. Rxe5 (23. Nf3 {is also good}) 23... Rxe5 24. Rxe5 Ng4 25.
Re6+ {starting a slide} (25. Ne4+ {considered by Wh to keep the K back} Kf7 26.
Ra5 $18 Nxh2 (26... Ra8 27. Ra3 (27. Nd6+ Kg7 28. Nxb7) 27... Ke7 (27... Nxh2
28. Rh3 Nf1 29. Rxh7+ Ke6 30. Rxb7) 28. h3 Nf6 29. Nxf6 Kxf6 30. Kd2 $18) 27.
Rxa7 $18 {SF16}) 25... Kf5 26. g3 $2 {loses a N} h6 27. Re7 {just hoping to
collect pawns in compensation} (27. Nf7 Kxe6 28. Nxh8 Kf6 {trapped N}) 27...
hxg5 28. fxg5 Rxh2 29. Rxb7 a5 $2 {Wh gets very good play now} (29... Ne3 $1
30. Rxa7 (30. c3 {just doesn't feel right} Ke4 31. a4 Rh1+ 32. Kd2 Rh2+ 33. Ke1
Nc4 34. b4 a6) 30... Rxc2+ 31. Kb1 Rg2 32. a4 Nc4 33. Rb7 Rxg3 34. Rb4 (34. b4
