36. Kc2 Nc4 $19 {SF16- the Wh K is still in trouble}) 30. Ra7 Ne3 (30... Ne5
31. Rxa5 Rg2 {just holding on to pawns is best- the race between the g and a
pawns should favour the g pawn, which has extra support} 32. a4 Rxg3 33. Ra8
Rxg5 34. a5 Kf4 35. a6 (35. b4 Rf5 36. Rd8 Rf7 37. c4 Ke4 38. Kb2 (38. b5 Nxc4
39. bxc6 Nxa5 40. Rc8 g5 $19)) 35... Rf5 36. a7 Rf7 37. Kd2 g5 38. Ke2 g4 39.
Kf2 g3+ 40. Kg2 Nc4 41. Re8 Rxa7 42. Rf8+ Ke4 43. Kxg3 Nxb2 {and the last Bl
pawn wins}) 31. Rxa5+ Kg4 {going for an attack on the K, but the safety of the
Bl pawns is crucial.After the text Wh was seeing at least a draw, and quite
likely winning chances with the Q side pawns} (31... Ke6 32. Rc5 Kd6 33. b4 Rg2
34. a4 Rxg3 35. a5 Nd5 36. Rc4 Rxg5 37. a6 Rf5 38. Rg4 Kc7 (38... g5) 39. Rxg6
Nxb4 40. Rg7+ Kd6 41. a7 Ra5 $19) 32. Rc5 Kf3 $11 (32... Rh1+ {best try Sf16}
33. Kd2 Nf1+ 34. Kd3 Nxg3 35. a4 Rd1+ 36. Kc4 Ne4 37. Rxc6 Kxg5 38. a5 Kf5 39.
a6 g5 40. Kb5 Ra1 41. Rc7 g4 42. Rf7+ Nf6 43. Rg7 Nh5 44. Rd7 g3 45. Rd2 Kf4 (
45... Nf4 46. Kb6 g2 47. Rxg2 Nxg2 48. a7 Ne3 49. Kb7 $11) 46. Kb6 Ke3 47. Rg2
Kf3 48. Rxg3+ Nxg3 49. a7 $11) 33. Rxc6 {a Rxg6 now assures a draw at least
for Wh} Ke2 34. b4 $16 Rg2 35. Rxg6 {deciding to have a the draw confirmed,
but makes life more difficult} (35. b5 Rxg3 36. b6 (36. Rxg6 Nc4 $11) 36...
Rxg5 37. a4 {considered, but got not much further} Rg1+ 38. Kb2 Rg4 39. Kb3 Rg1
40. c4 g5 41. a5 Ra1 42. Rg6 g4 43. Rg7 Kd3 44. Rd7+ Ke4 45. b7 Rb1+ 46. Kc3 g3
47. a6 g2 48. Rg7 Ke5 49. Rxg2 Nxg2 50. a7 $18 {Sf16}) 35... Nc4 36. Re6+ Kf3
37. Re1 (37. c3 {SF16} Rxg3 (37... Rxa2 38. g6 Rg2 39. b5 Rxg3 40. b6 Na5 41.
Re5 Nc6 42. Rc5 Rxg6 43. b7 Nb8 44. Rc8 Na6 45. Ra8 $18) 38. Rc6 Ne5 39. Rd6
Nc4 (39... Rg2 40. a4 Ke3 41. a5 Nc4 42. Rh6 Rxg5 43. Kc2 Rg2+ 44. Kb3 Nd2+ 45.
Ka4 Kd3 46. a6 Ne4 47. Ka5 Nxc3 {and the tablebases confirm this is a drawn
