1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. c3 Nc6 (3... e6) 4. Bf4 Bf5 5. Nbd2 e6 6. h3 Bd6 7. Ne5
Ne4 $146 (7... Bxe5 8. dxe5 Nd7 9. Nf3 Be4 $17 {SF16; 1-2-2}) 8. Nxc6 bxc6 9.
Bxd6 Qxd6 (9... cxd6 $15 {SF16-is a useful pawn mass in the centre, whick
keeps Wh's pieces away from squares they might otherwise occupy}) 10. e3 $11
Rb8 11. Qc1 h5 {Bl is far better developed, but the position is still closed}
12. Be2 h4 (12... g5 {interesting idea from SF16}) 13. Bf3 Ng5 14. Bd1 Ne4 15.
Bf3 Nxd2 16. Qxd2 Rh6 17. Rc1 e5 (17... Rg6 $11) 18. dxe5 Qxe5 19. b3 (19. O-O
$14) 19... Rd6 20. Qd4 Qxd4 21. cxd4 a5 $11 {though Wh can try to make
something of his pressure on the c file} 22. O-O g5 23. Kh2 (23. Rc5 Ra8 24.
Rfc1 Kd7 25. Be2 $14 {SF16}) 23... a4 24. Bd1 (24. bxa4 Rb4 25. a3 (25. Bd1 Rb2
26. Bb3 Bd3 27. Rfd1 Be4 28. Rf1 (28. Kg1 g4 29. a5 Rg6 $19 {SF16}) 28... Bd3
$11) 25... Rxa4 26. Rc3 Rc4 27. Rfc1 Bd3 28. a4 Kd7 29. a5 Rh6 30. Rxc4 dxc4 (
30... Bxc4 31. Bg4+ $16) 31. a6 Rh8 32. Ra1 Ra8 $11 {SF16}) 24... Bd3 25. Re1
axb3 26. Bxb3 Rf6 (26... Kd7) 27. Red1 Be2 28. Rd2 Bh5 29. Bd1 Bg6 30. Ba4 Kd7
31. Rc5 Rd6 32. Bd1 Ra8 (32... Rb1 $11 {SF16}) 33. a4 $16 f5 34. Ra2 (34. a5)
34... f4 35. Bg4+ Ke7 36. a5 fxe3 37. fxe3 $16 Bd3 38. Rf2 (38. Ra3 Be4 39. a6
Rf6 40. Ra2 Ra7 41. Bc8 Bd3 42. e4 Bb1 43. Rd2 Bxe4 44. Bb7 Kd8 $14 {SF16- Bl
has a R stuck on a7. However as soon as the wh Rs try to get into the game via
the other side, then a Bd3 will release that a7 R}) 38... Ra6 39. Bh5 (39. Bc8
Ra7 40. a6 Rg6 41. Ra5 Rg7 42. Bb7 $18 {here Wh already has a R on the f file,
poised to enter} Rf7 43. Rxf7+ Kxf7 44. Kg1 Ke7 45. Kf2 Bb5 46. Kf3 Kf6 47. Ra3
Bc4 48. Ra5 Bb5 49. e4 dxe4+ 50. Kxe4 Ke6 51. Kf3 Kf6 {the Engine insists that
Wh is winning, but keeps on probing. Lets try nudging the Engine} 52. Ra2 Ke6 (
52... Kf5 53. Bc8+ Kf6 54. Kg4 c5 55. dxc5 Bc4 56. Rf2+ Kg6 57. Bb7 Bd3 58. Rd2
Bxa6 59. Ra2 Rxb7 60. Rxa6+ Kf7 61. Kxg5 {and with a far more active R & K Wh
is clearly winning}) 53. Kg4 Kd5 54. Kxg5 Kxd4 55. Kxh4 c5 56. g4 Bd3 57. g5 c4
58. Rg2 Bg6 59. Rg4+ Kc5 60. Rg1 c3 61. Kg4 Kd6 62. h4 c2 63. h5 Bd3 64. g6
Be2+ 65. Bf3 Bxa6 66. Rc1 Bd3 67. g7 $18 {SF16 nudged}) 39... Rf6 40. Bf3 Bb5
41. Ra2 Bc4 42. Kg1 {time ?} (42. Ra3 Kd6 43. Bg4 Rf2 44. Bc8 Ra8 45. Bb7 Rb8
46. a6 Bxa6 47. Bxa6 Rbb2 48. Rac3 Rxg2+ 49. Kh1 Rh2+ 50. Kg1 Rbg2+ 51. Kf1 Ke7
52. Rxc6 Kd8 53. Ke1 Rxh3 54. Bf1 Rh1 55. R3c5 Rgg1 56. Rxd5+ Kc8 57. Rf6 g4
$14 {and SF16 here finds only a small advantage for Wh}) 42... Bxa2 $19 43. Be2
Bc4 44. Bf3 Rf8 45. e4 dxe4 46. Bxe4 Rf1+ (46... Bd5) 47. Kh2 Bb5 48. d5 Kd6
49. Rxc6+ Bxc6 50. Bd3 Rxa5 0-1

