1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Nxd7 5. Nc3 (5. O-O) (5. c4 {main lines
}) 5... Ngf6 6. d3 e6 {110 games 29% for Wh} (6... g6 {130 games,31% for Wh})
7. O-O Be7 8. Re1 O-O 9. e5 (9. h3 {25 games, 52% for Wh}) (9. Bf4 {14 gmes,
61 % for Wh}) 9... dxe5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 Qd4 (11... Bd6 {1-1-2}) 12. Rg5
(12. Re1 c4 13. dxc4 Qxc4 14. Qe2 Rac8 {Radovic-Djordjeviv, SRB Central ch
2016,0-1}) 12... a6 (12... Nd5 13. Nxd5 {Singe-Otim, Nairobi op, 2016,0-1}) 13.
Be3 Qh4 14. g3 (14. Qf3 $11 {SF16}) 14... Qh3 $2 (14... Qb4 15. Bd2 Qb6 16. Re5
Qc6 17. b3 b5 $15 {SF16}) 15. d4 $2 (15. Ne4 $18 g6 (15... Nxe4 16. Rh5 $18)
16. Nxf6+ Bxf6 17. Rxc5 {SF16}) 15... cxd4 (15... h6 $1 16. Re5 Ng4 $19 {SF16})
16. Bxd4 h6 $2 (16... Rfd8 $19 {SF16}) 17. Bxf6 hxg5 18. Bxe7 $18 Rfe8 19. Bxg5
Kh7 20. Qd3+ g6 21. Qf3 (21. Ne4 $1 {exploits the bl square weaknesses} e5 (
21... Rec8 22. Qd4 e5 23. Qxe5 Rc6 24. Nf6+ Rxf6 25. Bxf6 Qe6 26. Qg5 $18) 22.
Nf6+ (22. Qd5) 22... Kg7 23. Nxe8+ Rxe8 24. Qf3 $18 {SF16}) 21... f5 (21... Qf5
$5) 22. Qxb7+ Kg8 23. Bf6 (23. Re1 $1 {brings the last piece into the game} Qh5
24. h4 Qh7 25. Qxh7+ Kxh7 26. Na4 Rac8 27. c3 Rc6 28. Rd1 $18 {SF16- 2 pices
and two pawns against a R, & Bl is still got holes around the K position})
23... Qh7 24. Qxh7+ Kxh7 25. Rd1 Kh6 26. Rd7 (26. h4 $1 {keeps Bl's pawns back
ward}) 26... g5 27. h4 gxh4 28. Bxh4 Kh5 29. Re7 {Wh should keep Rs on for the
moment as his R is better than either of Bl's} (29. Kg2 Rab8 30. b3 Rbc8 31.
Ne2 Rxc2 32. Nf4+ Kh6 33. Rd6 Rxa2 34. Nxe6 $18 {SF16- Bl has to be careful
not to get mated} Kh7 35. Bf6 Kg8 36. Bd4 (36. Nd4) 36... Re2 37. Ng5 Kf8 38.
Rf6+ Ke7 39. Rxa6 Rg8 40. Bc5+ Kd7 41. Nf3 Re4 42. Nd4 Rg5 43. Kf3 Rh5 44. Ra7+
Kc8 45. b4 {SF16- Bl's R can find little to do while Wh slowly advances, after
picking off the f5 pawn as well}) 29... Rxe7 30. Bxe7 Kg4 31. Kg2 Ra7 32. Bf6 (
32. Bd6 {covers f4}) 32... Rd7 33. a4 Rd2 34. b4 (34. Be5 Rxc2 35. Nd1 Rc1 36.
Ne3+ Kg5 37. a5 Rc5 38. f4+ Kg6 39. Bc3 {SF16- everything is protected and Wh
advances the K into the centre , then wins more pawns before the final advance}
) 34... Rxc2 35. b5 axb5 36. axb5 Rb2 37. Be5 $18 {this should be quite
comfotable as well, though Wh could do with getting his K active} Rb3 (37...
Rc2 38. b6 Rb2 39. Nd5 Rb3 40. Nf6+ Kg5 41. Nd7 Rb4 42. Bf4+ Kg6 43. Bc7 Kf7
44. Ne5+ Ke8 45. Kf3 {SF16-heading over to the Q side to support the b pawn})
38. Bd4 (38. f3+ Kg5 39. Kf2 Rb2+ 40. Ke3 Rb4 41. Bd6 Rb2 42. Kd4 Rf2 43. b6
Rb2 44. Kc5) 38... Rb4 39. Bf6 Rb3 (39... f4) 40. f3+ Kh5 41. Kf2 Kg6 42. Be5
Kf7 43. Ke3 Ke7 44. Kd3 (44. Kd4) 44... Rb4 45. Bd4 Kd7 46. g4 {Wh should
leave the K side pawns alone-keep pawns on when going for a win. The Q side
should be the scene of battle} (46. Bc5 Rb2 47. f4 Rg2 48. Kc4 Rxg3 49. Bd4 Kc8
50. Na4 Rf3 51. Be5 Kb7 52. Nc5+ Kb6 53. Nxe6 Ra3 54. Bd4+ Kb7 55. b6 Ka6 56.
Nd8 (56. Kd5 {though Wh can pick up the f5 pawn at any time}) 56... Ra5 57. b7
Rb5 58. Be5 Ka7 59. b8=Q+ Rxb8 60. Bxb8+ Kxb8 61. Kd5 Kc8 62. Ne6 Kd7 63. Ke5 {
SF16}) 46... fxg4 47. fxg4 e5 48. Ba7 Rxg4 {without the extra pawns it has
become more difficult. And Wh also needs to know how to mate with a B & N vs K}
49. b6 (49. Bc5 $18 Rf4 50. Kc2 Rh4 51. Kb3 Kc7 52. Nd5+ Kd7 53. Bb4 Rh2 54.
Ka4 Ra2+ 55. Ba3 Rh2 56. Ka5 Ra2 57. Kb4 Ra1 58. Nb6+ Ke6 59. Nc4 e4 60. Ne3 {
The Engine knows how to win this, but Bl has gained a lot of activity}) 49...
Kc6 $11 {the B is cut off from the centre} 50. Ne4 Kb7 51. Nc5+ Ka8 52. Nd7 $2
(52. Ke3 Rc4 $11) 52... Rd4+ 53. Ke3 Rxd7 $19 54. Ke4 Re7 55. Ke3 Kb7 (55... e4
{keeps the B away from the B, then Bl brings the K up while the R stops the B
pawn from advancing}) 56. Ke4 Kc6 $2 (56... Re8 57. Kd3 e4+ 58. Ke3 Re7 $19 {
repeating the process to Q the pawn}) 57. Bb8 Kxb6 58. Bxe5 $11 {Bl can only
win this if the B gets pinned against the K on the back rank, or the K gets
trapped in a corner} Kc6 59. Kf5 (59. Kd4 {keeps the K in the centre, a much
safer place}) 59... Kd5 60. Bg3 Rf7+ 61. Kg4 (61. Kg5) 61... Ke4 62. Bh4 (62.
Kg5) 62... Rg7+ 63. Bg5 Rg8 64. Kh4 Kf5 65. Bd2 Ke4 66. Bg5 Kf3 67. Kh5 Kg3 68.
Kh6 (68. Be3 {stays away from the corner}) 68... Kg4 69. Bf6 Kf5 70. Bg7 Rxg7
71. Kxg7 1/2-1/2

