axb3 exd4 16. Nxd4 Nxd4 17. cxd4 c5 18. d5 $14 {SF16}) 15. cxd4 d5 16. e5 $16
Nh7 17. Nf1 Na5 18. Bc2 $18 Nc4 19. Qd3 (19. Bc1) 19... Nf8 20. Rab1 c5 21.
dxc5 (21. Bf4) 21... Bxc5 (21... d4 22. Bxd4 Bxc5 23. b4 Nxe5 24. Rxe5 Bd6 25.
Ng3 Bxe5 26. Nxe5 Rxd4 27. Qxd4 Qxc2 $11 {SF16}) 22. Bxc5 Qxc5 23. Nd4 $18 {
Bl has an inferior B & an isolated QP. Also Wh can easily advance pawns on the
K side} g6 24. Nxe6 {but this gets rid of a major Bl weakness} (24. f4 Re8 25.
Ng3 Qe7 26. Re2 f5 27. b3 Na3 28. Rd1 b4 29. Red2 Nb5 30. Nxb5 axb5 31. Bb1 Nd7
32. Qxb5 $18 {SF16- the other N can also get to d4}) 24... Nxe6 $11 25. Ng3 $2
(25. Qg3 Qd4 26. b3 Na3 27. Rbd1 Qf4 28. Qxf4 Nxf4 29. Bd3 Rac8 $11 {SF16})
25... Nf4 (25... Qxf2 $19) (25... Rac8 26. Qe2 Qd4 27. Kg1 Nf4 28. Qd1 Qxd1 29.
Bxd1 Nd3 $19 {SF16}) 26. Qf3 $16 Ne6 (26... g5 27. Rbc1 Nd2 28. Qe3 Qxe3 29.
fxe3 (29. Rxe3 d4 $19) 29... Ne6 30. b3 $16 {SF16}) 27. Qf6 $18 Nf8 (27... Nxe5
